1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,067
How is a computer chip made? In six
stages, from sand to silicon.

2
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,958
A semiconductor controls the flow of
electricity.

3
00:00:09,958 --> 00:00:12,951
It sits between a conductor and an
insulator.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,224
One. Purify. Silica from sand becomes
ultra-pure silicon.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,751
Two. Wafer.

6
00:00:21,751 --> 00:00:26,803
The silicon grows into a crystal ingot,
then it's sliced into thin wafers.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:28,930
Three. Pattern.

8
00:00:28,930 --> 00:00:33,269
UV light shines through a mask, and prints
the circuit onto the wafer.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,632
Four. Layers. Etching, doping and
deposition build the circuit, one layer at
a time.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,529
Five. Wire and inspect.

11
00:00:43,529 --> 00:00:47,717
Metal pathways connect the parts, and
defects are caught early.

12
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,419
Six. Package and test. Each chip is cut
and sealed, then tested, before it ships.

13
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:59,727
Quick check. Particles are rising in the
cleanroom. What do you do?

14
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:06,376
Pause, and investigate. Catching it early
saves the whole batch.

15
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:11,308
Six stages. One rule throughout:
precision.
